course: dictionary
lesson: 9813
title: Sway: moving, changing minds, and power
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sway is a word with three meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. Read the clues before you choose. «The trees swayed in the breeze» is about movement: the trees moved slowly from side to side.
explain: Sway can also mean to change someone's mind. «The advert tried to sway me to buy the new trainers» means it tried to make me decide to buy them. Check by swapping in a meaning: "make me decide" fits the sentence, so this is the right meaning.
explain: Sway as a noun means power or influence over people, as in the phrase «hold sway». A famous singer can hold sway over her fans. The clues are people, power and influence.
fact: Sway (verb) means to move slowly from side to side.
fact: To sway someone means to change their opinion or make them decide something.
fact: Sway (noun) means power or influence over people, as in «hold sway».
fact: The other forms are «swayed» and «swaying»: «the boat swayed on the waves», «quiet water-lilies swaying on the surface of an English stream».
fact: Tall buildings and bridges are often built to sway a little in wind or earthquakes, so they do not break.
exercise: «The tall grass swayed in the warm wind.» What does swayed mean here? | *Moved slowly from side to side | Shouted loudly | Turned into hay | Was cut down
exercise: «The advert tried to sway me to buy the new trainers.» What does sway mean here? | Fall asleep | Make a loud noise | Move slowly from side to side | *Change someone's opinion or make them decide
exercise: Which meaning is in the phrase «hold sway»? | Standing very still | *Power or influence over people | Moving slowly from side to side | Changing your mind
test: «The boat swayed on the waves.» What does swayed mean? | *Rocked slowly from side to side | Stayed perfectly still | Sailed very fast | Sank to the bottom
test: Jade says the advert wants to sway her. What does Jade mean? | The advert is very sad | *The advert wants to change her mind | The advert wants to dance with her | The advert wants to hit her
exam: In «the singer held sway over the crowd», what does sway mean? | *Power or influence over people | Moving slowly from side to side | Changing the rhythm of a song | Sitting down in the crowd
